# What the image build must NOT be sent.
#
# `Containerfile` runs `COPY . .` twice — once for the cargo-chef planner and
# once for the builder — so every path listed here is one that would otherwise
# cross into the build context on both. `target/` alone is several gigabytes of
# host-architecture artifacts that the musl build cannot use and immediately
# overwrites, and `.git/` carries the whole history of a repository the image
# never reads.
#
# A DENY LIST rather than an allow list, deliberately. An allow list that forgets
# a file the build needs fails at compile time with a missing-module error three
# stages deep, and the next person adding a source directory has to remember to
# amend it. Everything named below is something the build provably does not read.
#
# `.dockerignore` rather than `.containerignore`: docker reads only the former,
# and podman and buildah fall back to it when no `.containerignore` exists — so
# one file covers every builder this repository is built with.

# Build output. The largest single entry by far, and the only one worth
# measuring: the musl target the image ships is built inside the container.
target/

# History, hooks and the remote configuration. Nothing in the build reads them.
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# CI and review artifacts. `.local-review/` is a local review tool's scratch
# output — it is ignored by git and must not reach an image either.
.github/
.local-review/
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Deployment and documentation. The chart is applied by Argo from the repository,
# never from inside the image.
chart/
README.md

# Formatting configuration, which only the pre-commit hooks read.
.prettierrc
.prettierignore

# `cargo deny` configuration, which runs in CI rather than in the image build.
deny.toml
